# Backend architecture

Layer call direction (strict):

`Controller → Service → Repository → Persistence`

## Allowed dependencies

| Layer | May call |
|---|---|
| Controllers | Services, Dto |
| Services | Repositories, Domain, Dto |
| Repositories | Persistence, Domain |
| Domain | (nothing outward) |
| Dto | (nothing outward) |
| Persistence | Domain |
| Middleware | infrastructure / cross-cutting only |

## Forbidden

- Repositories must never call Services (or Controllers)
- Controllers must never call Repositories or Persistence directly
- Domain must not reference Controllers, Services, Repositories, Middleware, Dto, or Persistence
- Dto must not reference Controllers, Services, Repositories, Middleware, or Persistence
- Domain stays free of Express/Fastify/Node HTTP types; use Dto at the API boundary

## Testing

- Every backend interaction must have tests
- New or changed Controllers and Services require corresponding unit or integration tests under `tests/Backend/`
- Layer boundaries are enforced by `tests/Backend/Architecture.Tests` — keep those rules green
- Do not add interaction code without tests
